IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-8), Part I, Divisions A and B (sections 5 to 20) -- piece cp1.
-- THE NOUNS: the records and the enumeration that more than one cp1 module shares. Declarations only.
--
-- The text this encoding reads is an unofficial plain-text rendering made by a converter script from the
-- Justice Laws consolidation; nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- Conventions (see NOTES.md and the keel's cpp-core.l4): money is a NUMBER of Canadian dollars; a rate is a
-- fraction (5.95% is 0.0595); a year is a NUMBER; a month is the DATE of its first day (YMD y m 1).
-- Every type here begins with the piece code cp1, as the keel's naming conventions ask.

§ `Part I, Divisions A and B -- the nouns cp1 shares`

§§ `A run of months`

-- Several provisions count months: "each month excluded from the contributory period by reason of
-- disability" (sections 12, 13, 17, 17.1, 19). The excluded months are a run (or several runs) of months.
-- Both ends are the first day of a month. A run with no end has not ended.
DECLARE `cp1 Month period` HAS
    `first month of the month period` IS A DATE
    `last month of the month period` IS A MAYBE DATE

§§ `The facts about one person that decide which months of a year count`

-- Sections 12, 13, 17, 17.1 and 19 all turn on the same events in a person's life: reaching eighteen or
-- seventy, dying, the end of the contributory period by reason of disability, the disability pension ceasing to be
-- payable, a retirement pension becoming payable, and the elections of subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii) and
-- paragraphs 13(1)(b) and (c). One record carries them, so that the five sections cannot disagree about a fact.
--
-- A MAYBE DATE field is NOTHING when the event has not happened. A person who has made, revoked or been
-- through the event more than once calls the rules with the occurrence that matters for the year at hand
-- (NOTES.md, fork register).
--
-- out of range: section 49 (piece cp3): the contributory period, and the months excluded from it by reason of disability.
-- out of range: section 70 (piece cp5): a disability pension ceasing to be payable.
-- out of range: section 44 (piece cp3) and section 67 (piece cp5): a retirement pension becoming payable.
-- out of range: regulations 83.1 and 83.2 (piece cr1): the form and manner in which the elections of subsection 12(1.1) and subsection 13(1.1) are made and revoked.
DECLARE `cp1 Facts about a person for a year` HAS
    `the year at hand` IS A NUMBER
    `date of birth of the person` IS A DATE
    `date of death of the person` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `date the contributory period of the person ends by reason of disability` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `date the disability pension ceases to be payable to the person` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `months excluded from the contributory period of the person by reason of disability` IS A LIST OF `cp1 Month period`
    `month from which a retirement pension is payable to the person` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `date the person makes an election under subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii)` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `date the person revokes the election under subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii)` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `month referred to in the election of the person under paragraph 13(1)(b)` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `month referred to in the revocation by the person under paragraph 13(1)(c)` IS A MAYBE DATE

§§ `The one election event of a year`

-- Paragraphs 17(b) and (c) (and 17.1, 19 and 13(1)(b) to (e)) each name the election made or deemed made,
-- and the election revoked or deemed revoked, "for a year in which" it happens. Subsections 12(1.1)(d) to (f)
-- and 13(1.1)(b) to (d) bar two events of the same kind in one year; the text does not say what happens if
-- an election of one kind is made and an election of the other kind is revoked in one year. That case is the
-- constructor `more than one election event in the year`, and the rules that need the event answer NOTHING for it.
DECLARE `cp1 Election event in a year` IS ONE OF
    `no election event in the year`
    `an election under subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii) is made in the year`
    `an election under subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii) is revoked in the year`
    `an election under paragraph 13(1)(b) is deemed made in the year`
    `an election under paragraph 13(1)(c) is deemed revoked in the year`
    `more than one election event in the year`

§§ `Income received on a date`

-- Subsection 12(1) excludes "any such income received by the person" before eighteen, in an excluded month,
-- after sixty-five under an election, and after seventy. Whether income is excluded depends on the date it
-- was received, so the income is a list of receipts.
DECLARE `cp1 Income receipt` HAS
    `date the income is received` IS A DATE
    `amount of the income received` IS A NUMBER

§§ `One employment of an employee in a year`

-- Subsections 8(4) to (11) prorate the basic exemption and the maximums over "each pensionable employment",
-- some under this Act and some under a provincial pension plan.
DECLARE `cp1 Employment of an employee in a year` HAS
    `contributory salary and wages of the employee from the employment` IS A NUMBER
    `the provisions of this Act relating to the making of contributions apply to the employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the provisions of a provincial pension plan apply to the employment` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `One business of a person in a year`

-- Section 14(a) takes the income of all businesses, except a business more than half of whose gross revenue
-- is rent, and except income or losses from services described in paragraph 7(1)(d) that a regulation has
-- included in pensionable employment.
DECLARE `cp1 Business carried on by a person` HAS
    `income of the person for the year from the business` IS A NUMBER
    `losses sustained by the person in the year in carrying on the business` IS A NUMBER
    `more than fifty per cent of the gross revenue of the business consisted of rent from land or buildings` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the income or losses are from services described in paragraph 7(1)(d) that a regulation has included in pensionable employment` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `One employment: the facts sections 6 and 7 turn on`

-- Section 6 says what is pensionable employment and what is excepted employment. The eleven kinds of excepted
-- employment in subsection 6(2) each turn on a few plain facts about the employment; one record carries them.
-- out of range: regulation 2(2) (piece cr1): the industry words of paragraph 6(2)(a) and "international organization" in paragraph 6(2)(j).
-- out of range: regulations 15 to 35, Part III of the Regulations (piece cr1), made under section 7: whether a regulation includes or excepts the employment.
-- out of range: the Indian Act and the Income Tax Act are not part of this text: "Indian", and income that is or is not included for tax.
DECLARE `cp1 Facts about an employment` HAS
    `the employment is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employment is under Her Majesty in right of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a regulation made under section 7 includes the employment in pensionable employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a regulation made under section 7 excepts the employment from pensionable employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employment is in agriculture or an agricultural enterprise, horticulture, fishing, hunting, trapping, forestry, logging or lumbering` IS A BOOLEAN
    `cash remuneration the employer pays the employee in the year` IS A NUMBER
    `the employer employs the employee on terms providing for payment of cash remuneration` IS A BOOLEAN
    `working days in the year for which the employer so employs the employee` IS A NUMBER
    `the employment is of a casual nature` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employment is for the purpose of the employer's trade or business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employee is a teacher on exchange from a country other than Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employee is employed by the employee's spouse or common-law partner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the remuneration paid may be deducted under the Income Tax Act in computing the income of the spouse or common-law partner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employee is a member of a religious order who has taken a vow of perpetual poverty` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the remuneration is paid either directly or by the member to the order` IS A BOOLEAN
    `no cash remuneration is paid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employee is the child of the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employee is maintained by the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employment is as a member of the Canadian Forces or the Royal Canadian Mounted Police` IS A BOOLEAN
    `another Act of Parliament provides otherwise for that employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employer employs persons in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a reciprocal agreement between the Government of Canada and the government of another country exempts the employer from liability to make the contributions imposed on an employer by this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employment is by Her Majesty in right of a province or by an agent of Her Majesty in right of a province` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employment is by the government of a country other than Canada or by an international organization` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employee is an Indian as defined in the Indian Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the earnings from the employment are not included in computing income for the purposes of the Income Tax Act` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `One employee's contributions in a year, under this Act and under a provincial pension plan`

-- Subsection 8(2) asks whether the amounts deducted from an employee's remuneration for a year, "whether by one or
-- more employers", under this Act or a provincial pension plan, exceed what the employee had to contribute; and
-- subsections 8(4) to (11) prorate the exemption and the maximums over the employee's several employments.
-- The record carries everything those subsections read. A rate or maximum that a paragraph does not use for the
-- year at hand (the first additional rate before 2019, the second additional rate before 2024) is ignored there.
--
-- out of range: Schedule 1 and Schedule 2 (piece cp6): the rates under this Act.
-- out of range: a provincial pension plan is not part of this text: the plan's own rates.
-- out of range: section 21 (piece cp2) and regulations 5 and 6 (piece cr1): the amounts deducted from the remuneration.
-- Sections 16 to 20 are in this piece (cp1-div-b-maximum-earnings-and-exemption.l4): the caller passes their results,
-- including the "without paragraphs 17(b) and (c)" variants that subsections 8(6), (7), (10) and (11) ask for.
DECLARE `cp1 Facts about the contributions of an employee for a year` HAS
    `the year at hand` IS A NUMBER
    `employments of the employee in the year` IS A LIST OF `cp1 Employment of an employee in a year`
    `contributory self-employed earnings of the employee for the year, if the employee is an individual described in section 10 to whom the provisions relating to the making of contributions apply` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the contribution rate for employees for the year under this Act` IS A NUMBER
    `the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year under this Act` IS A NUMBER
    `the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year under this Act` IS A NUMBER
    `the base contribution rate for employees for the year under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER
    `the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER
    `the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER
    `the employee's basic exemption for the year` IS A NUMBER
    `the employee's basic exemption for the year, determined without taking into account paragraphs 19(b) and (c)` IS A NUMBER
    `the employee's maximum contributory earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER
    `the employee's maximum contributory earnings for the year, determined without taking into account paragraphs 17(b) and (c) and 19(b) and (c)` IS A NUMBER
    `the employee's maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER
    `the employee's maximum pensionable earnings for the year, determined without taking into account paragraphs 17(b) and (c)` IS A NUMBER
    `the employee's additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER
    `the employee's additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year, determined without taking into account paragraphs 17.1(b) and (c)` IS A NUMBER
    `aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of the employee for the year on account of the employee's contributions under this Act` IS A NUMBER
    `aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of the employee for the year on account of the employee's contributions under this Act or under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER

§§ `A figure Statistics Canada has published`

-- Subsection 18(6) uses the revision of the Wage Measure "that has been published most recently prior to the calculation".
DECLARE `cp1 Published figure` HAS
    `date the figure is published` IS A DATE
    `the published figure` IS A NUMBER
